## Model routing

Each persona pins its common-case model in `model:`. {{role:architect}} can override per dispatch.

**Principle:** the cheapest model that gets the task right first time. Rework (a review bounce, a fix round) costs more than the stronger model would have.

| Tier | Model | Tasks |
|---|---|---|
| fast | `{{models.fast}}` | mechanical, fully specified: link checks, label hygiene, simple renames |
| balanced | `{{models.balanced}}` | writing from clear sources: docs deltas, process edits, routine reviews |
| strong | `{{models.strong}}` | judgement and design: building with TDD, domain design, tricky reviews, nuanced copy |
| strongest | `{{models.strongest}}` | security and risky calls |

<!-- render: one line listing each enabled agent and its tier → model -->

- **Measure and adapt.** Each dispatch is logged on the retro issue (agent · model · task type · bounced at review y/n). At each retro, a task type that bounces moves up a tier; one that never bounces is tried a tier lower.
- **Floor.** {{role:security}}'s reviews stay on the strongest tier.
- **A different model judges.** Where possible, the model that reviews a diff is not the one that wrote it.

### Report length
Every report to {{role:architect}} is **≤ 300 words**: outcome, SHAs, decisions needed, `## Feedback`. Evidence goes on the issue or PR. A review is ≤ 200 words per PR.

### Throughput
At most 2 agents in parallel unless their paths are disjoint; reviews are batched per agent.

